    {"id":"c7b419f1-43da-48b2-8012-4da48912a404","name":"Sticky Note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","typeVersion":1,"position":[100,300],"parameters":{"content":"## PLUTO — WhatsApp Channel Relay (SHARED across every branch's WhatsApp number)\nOne workflow, two entry points:\n1. WhatsApp Business Webhook — Meta calls this for both the GET verify handshake and every inbound message. It looks up the right clinic channel by phone_number_id (calling backend GET /channels?identifier=), then relays to /conversations/inbound and, if mode=ai, /chat/reply, then sends the reply straight to the Graph API using that channel's own decrypted access_token — never a static n8n credential, since every branch has its own WhatsApp number/token.\n2. Outbound Send Webhook — backend calls this (staff replies, reminders, recalls...) with {recipient, message, channel_identifier}; same per-channel token lookup, then sends via Graph API.\n\nBEFORE USE:\n- Replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_VERIFY_TOKEN in both IF nodes with a real secret string, and register that same string + this workflow's whatsapp-webhook URL in Meta App Dashboard -> WhatsApp -> Configuration -> Webhook.\n- Needs the \"PLUTO Service Token\" credential (template) wired to every \"Lookup Channel...\"/\"Send To Backend Inbound\"/\"Generate AI Reply\" HTTP Request node.\n- Update backend/app/routers/channels.py SHARED_N8N_WORKFLOWS[\"whatsapp\"] to (this workflow's id, \"whatsapp-outbound-send\").","color":6,"height":420,"width":520}}
